<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 69,683 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 69,683 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 69,683 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 39,351 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					   Tuesday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 9,231	    17,293</p>
<p>    Import cargo			60,452	    22,058</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven ships were expected to sail and 13 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	     Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 36,000	 Yasmeen		 7/5</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Warbah		  due</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Keefan		  due</p>
<p>Jet A-1 fuel	   25,000	 Chilham Castle	7/5</p>
<p>Chemicals		10,000	 San Mated	     5/5</p>
<p>Chemicals		 2,000	 Owl Trader	    due</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 25,000	 Al-Safa		 5/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
